link2symlink: leave the file untouched when a link fails

Hard-link emulation renamed the file away before creating the symbolic
links meant to stand in for it. On a filesystem that refuses symbolic
links -- Android shared storage answers EPERM -- the rename had already
happened: the caller's file was gone (left as `.l2s.<name>0001.0002`),
and the rename fallback git then tries failed with ENOENT ("unable to
rename temporary '*.pack' file"). The links are now created first and
every completed step is undone on failure, so a refused link fails the
way the kernel's own would, with the file where it was.

Also: the l2s_* helpers return -1 with errno set; that -1 was passed to
the tracee as is, turning every failure into EPERM. They now answer
-errno.

Upstream: termux/proot v5.1.107.92. Applied by app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.

